16. Security Design
The system should:
•	Keep Gemini/API credentials on the server.
•	Never expose secret API keys in frontend code.
•	Authenticate API requests.
•	Validate user input.
•	Restrict project access to its owner.
•	Sanitize generated/user-provided content where appropriate.
•	Store passwords using secure password hashing rather than plaintext.
